# Web SEO: CMS copy on the server

Marketing copy that crawlers should index must not rely on client-only presenter state or in-component schema fallbacks alone. Visible text in the first HTML response should match what users see after hydration (see **web-seo-index** → JavaScript rendering mismatch).

## Load pattern (`+page.server.ts`)

1. Call `configRepository.getPublicModuleConfig(...)` (stateless; safe on server).
2. Start from defaults helpers; overlay API values when non-empty.
3. Return VMs from the server load; pass through universal `+page.ts` into templates.

| Module | Defaults helper | Used for |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `landing_page` | `getLandingPageConfigDefaults()` | Hero, demo, landing FAQ **headers** |
| `public_faq` | `getPublicFaqConfigDefaults()` | FAQ section headers + Q&A **items** |

Parse FAQ with `parsePublicFaqConfigModule()` → `publicFaqConfigPm` / `publicFaqItemsVm` for `PublicFaq` and `createPublicFaqSEOSchema`.

## Landing vs pricing FAQ headers

- **Landing** (`/`): prefer `landing_page` `FAQ_*` fields in the UI; fall back to `public_faq`.
- **Pricing** (`/pricing`): `public_faq` only for FAQ headers.

Q&A item copy lives in `public_faq.ITEMS` (secret-admin **Public FAQ**, not Landing page). `publicFaqConfig.ts` (`PUBLIC_FAQ_ITEMS`) supplies code defaults when config is empty.

Default `items` is `PUBLIC_FAQ_ITEMS`; override only when a route renders a different FAQ list.

Stored `public_faq.ITEMS` **replaces** git defaults when non-empty. After changing default answers, re-save Public FAQ in admin (or clear `ITEMS`) so production matches `PUBLIC_FAQ_ITEMS`.

## FAQ answer links (landing + pricing accordion)

Answers are HTML. `FaqAccordion` runs `prepareBlogRichTextForDisplay` (internal followable; third-party `nofollow`) then `rewriteHtmlHostedMarketingHrefs` (self-host → `https://www.openquok.com/…` dofollow backlinks). JSON-LD `Answer.text` is **plain text** (`stripHtmlToPlainText` after the same rich-text prepare).

**Admin:** Public FAQ → ITEMS uses `FaqEditor` with Visual / HTML source (`richTextAnswers`). Questions stay plain text. Landing page config only edits FAQ **headers**.

Prefer **root-relative** `<a href="/docs/…">` (or Visual → link). Do not add `rel="nofollow"` on first-party anchors. One or two links per destination.

When adding or rewriting a landing/pricing FAQ answer, include a first-party link when the sentence names a surface:

| Topic | Typical href | Anchor |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Buffer / Hootsuite switch | `/compare/openquok/buffer`, `/blog/best-buffer-alternatives-for-teams-that-approve-ai-content-before-posting` | OpenQuok vs Buffer, Buffer alternatives guide |
| Trial / plan limits / seats | `/pricing` | Pricing |
| Schedule from CLI / agents | `/docs/getting-started-for-cli` | CLI getting started |
| Grok Bot | `/docs/agent-setup-guides/grok-bot`, `/blog/schedule-social-posts-from-grok-bot-with-openquok` | setup guide, walkthrough |
| Self-host | `/docs/installation/docker-compose`, `https://github.com/Ratimon/openquok-monorepo`, `/blog/how-to-self-host-openquok-with-cli-device-login-free-no-api-keys-on-your-agent` | Docker Compose, GitHub, device-login walkthrough |
| Agent hosts | `/agents`, `/docs/agent-setup-guides` | Agents, agent setup guides |
| MCP | `/docs/getting-started-for-mcp`, `/docs/mcp-setup-guides` | MCP getting started, MCP setup |
| Public API / OAuth / tokens | `/docs/getting-started-for-public-api`, `/docs/oauth2-for-apps` | Public API, OAuth2 for apps |
| Channels / official APIs | `/channels`, `/docs/social-integration` | Supported channels, channel setup guides |
| Channel groups | `/docs/apis-integrations/groups` | channel groups API |
| Analytics | `/docs/cli-usages/analytics` | analytics CLI |
| Threads / X comments | `/docs/cli-examples/threads`, `/docs/cli-examples/x` | Threads / X CLI examples |

Chrome Writer/Rewriter/Summarizer docs stay third-party (`nofollow` applied on display). Do not treat all of `github.com` as followable — only first-party `Ratimon/…` (see **web-seo-outbound-links**).

```html
<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<p>Follow the <a href="/docs/installation/docker-compose">Docker Compose self-host guide</a>.</p>

<!-- ❌ BAD — nofollow on a first-party docs path -->
<p>See <a href="/docs" rel="nofollow">docs</a>.</p>
```

## SEO parity

- FAQ JSON-LD (`createPublicFaqSEOSchema`) must use the **same** question text and the **plain-text** form of the visible accordion answer (link labels kept; tags stripped).
- Landing hero title/description from config feed both `createMetaData` and JSON-LD (`WebSite`, `Organization`).
- Demo section: `createLandingDemoSEOSchema` reads `DEMO_YOUTUBE_VIDEO_ID`, `DEMO_YOUTUBE_UPLOAD_DATE`, `DEMO_TITLE`, `DEMO_DESCRIPTION` from SSR `landing_page` config.

